:: DreamOfGathering [childhood]
# Visions of the Earth's Gifts

In your dream, you walk through meadows and forests you've never seen before. The landscape is vibrant with plant life - flowers in colors you've never imagined, trees heavy with fruit, roots and tubers pushing up through the soil as if offering themselves to you.

An old woman walks beside you, though you don't remember when she joined your journey. Her face is deeply lined, her hands gnarled like tree roots, but her eyes are bright with wisdom and knowledge.

"The plants speak," she tells you. "You must learn to listen."

She kneels beside a small, unremarkable plant with tiny white flowers. "This one heals fever," she says. Then points to another, "This strengthens the heart." And another, "This helps bring babies into the world safely."

As she speaks, you realize you can sense the plants' energies - some cool and soothing, others warm and invigorating, some with a quiet strength that builds slowly, others with immediate power.

"The earth provides everything we need," the old woman says. "But we must know where to look, when to harvest, and how to give thanks."

She places her hand on the ground, and you do the same. You feel a pulse beneath your palm - the heartbeat of the earth itself, connected to all living things.

"Remember," she says as the dream begins to fade, "plants are our oldest allies. Respect them, and they will sustain you."

You wake with the first light of dawn, the dream vivid in your mind. Your understanding of plants has deepened - they're not just food or materials, but living beings with their own wisdom and gifts to share.

